      "topic": "entry_window",
      "choice": "Interpreted 'October 1' as a recurring annual month/day threshold (month==10 and day>=1, or later months) checked every year in the 2020-2025 feed, since the spec gives no explicit year for the conversion event.",
      "reason": "The spec describes a single event but the backtest spans six years; a recurring seasonal filter is the only reading that lets the strategy operate across the full dataset."
    },
    {
      "topic": "entry_price_for_min_check",
      "choice": "Used the current bar's open price (the same price used in entry condition #4) as the 'asset price at time of entry' for the $160 skip rule.",
      "reason": "The spec does not define a distinct execution price separate from the signal-time open; the open is the only entry-time price available when the signal is evaluated."
    },
    {
      "topic": "position_sizing",
      "choice": "Sized the trade as notional value = 2% of current portfolio value, divided by the current close price, rather than risk-based sizing tied to the stop-loss distance.",
      "reason": "The spec states position size as a flat percentage of capital in a separate sentence from the stop-loss rule, not as risk-per-trade sizing."
    },
    {
      "topic": "stop_loss_trigger",
      "choice": "Checked the stop-loss using the intrabar high price (worst case for a short) and gave it priority over the closing-price-based exit conditions within the same bar.",
      "reason": "Stop-loss is a continuous risk-management mechanism, whereas the take-profit and SMA-reversal exits are explicitly defined in terms of the closing price."
    },
    {
